# UI test: a `tool` whose description opens with a blank `##` (SC0195).
#
# §5.2 takes the `title` from the first line of the run, which is the split
# `strings-formatting-and-docs.md` §5.4 already makes for its own reasons. A
# run that opens blank has no first line to be one.
#
# The distinction from SC0190 is the point: there *is* a description here, and
# all of it is sent. What is missing is the sentence a caller reading only the
# summary would see.

##
## Fit peaks in a time-of-flight window.
tool fit_peaks(run: String) -> Int:
    0
